    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/55264>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "it is accordingly obvious that in any two related individuals (whether specifically identical or not) the differences between them must manifest themselves gradually, and be but little apparent in the young. It is for the same simple reason that animals which are of very different sizes when adult, differ less and less in size (as well as in form) as we trace them backwards through the foetal stages.".
